1
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:08,940
(New Housemate Move-In Day)

2
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:10,800
Feels so dreamy today.

3
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,760
(Asks)
Were you born in 2000?

4
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:17,520
Yeah.

5
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:20,400
I remember you and Si

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,080
were born in 2000 too, right?

7
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:22,760
Yeah.

8
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,680
I think you two

9
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,880
are about two months younger than me.

10
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,160
You're a July baby?

11
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,880
Late May on the Chinese calendar,

12
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,920
late June on the regular one.

13
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:35,240
If I remember,

14
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,160
you're about...

15
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:38,400
two months younger than me.

16
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:39,440
Yeah.

17
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:39,840
Really?

18
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:40,360
Pretty much.

19
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:41,200
Three months.

20
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,040
A little over two months.

21
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:42,720
Yeah.

22
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:43,080
Well,

23
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:44,840
Si mentioned that to me before.

24
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,600
Everyone in the house

25
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,040
has a different personality.

26
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,000
Once you're in there tonight,

27
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,200
you'll see for yourself.

28
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:57,720
Okay.

29
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,460
But when I said I'd changed my name,

30
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:02,240
(Looks up)
you actually believed me.

31
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,000
That was...

32
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,400
pretty surprising.

33
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:06,620
(Laughs)

34
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:07,600
Because in his mind,

35
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,360
Si is someone

36
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,200
who would never lie.

37
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,800
- Right.
- He just trusts Si.

38
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,360
So,

39
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,360
I get where Sun Bohan was coming from.

40
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:13,760
Then

41
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,520
they asked me to introduce myself.

42
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,320
I thought

43
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,120
it felt kind of weird.

44
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,960
Something just felt off.

45
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,440
Yeah. Why introduce myself again?

46
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:23,100
(Smiles)

47
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:24,480
We kept laughing at you.

48
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,360
Did you catch on?

49
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,000
Yeah. When you laughed...

50
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:27,680
Something was off.

51
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,680
Yeah, more and more.

52
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,400
But he didn't notice.

53
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,640
Yeah, I still didn't catch on.

54
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,640
(Laughs)

55
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,680
If there's anything

56
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,840
you want to know about the house

57
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:39,760
but feel shy asking,

58
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:41,840
we can fill you in.

59
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:42,240
Yeah.

60
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:42,560
Okay.

61
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:45,800
I think she'll be fine.

62
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:46,920
I think...

63
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:47,760
she'll be okay.

64
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,760
Yeah.

65
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:50,960
So if...

66
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:51,720
you and Si

67
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:53,560
are both in front of us,

68
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,680
just smile.

69
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,680
I'll know you're Xingying right away.

70
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,520
You know?

71
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:58,000
Yeah.

72
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,960
(Laughs)

73
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,760
How long have you been in Beijing?

74
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,760
Over a year. Almost two.

75
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:08,440
So you came around the same time as Si.

76
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,240
So she...

77
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:09,880
Si has been here

78
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:12,000
a little over a year too.

79
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,200
Do you live in Beijing too?

80
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,200
You don't have a Beijing accent at all.

81
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,520
I've always sounded like this.

82
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:18,920
Honestly,

83
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,560
I don't know why I don't, but...

84
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:24,640
(Jumps in)
So tell me this.

85
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,280
Personality-wise,

86
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:27,680
how are Chen Hewen and I different?

87
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:29,880
Just your first impression.

88
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,200
You're both really friendly.

89
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:36,780
(Complimenting)

90
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:37,960
Of course.

91
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,360
We can't exactly

92
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,400
be unfriendly to you.

93
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:42,100
(Laughs)

94
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:45,480
Let's go.

95
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,320
Yeah, let's go.

96
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:50,100
(Back from the grocery store)

97
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,440
We...

98
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:53,600
we really love singing in this house.

99
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,480
We do.

100
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,000
And everyone's really good.

101
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,120
We're the Singing House.

102
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:58,720
Yep.

103
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,080
♪Look at this stuff♪

104
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,640
♪Isn't it neat♪

105
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,960
♪Up where they walk♪

106
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,640
♪Up where they run♪

107
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,680
♪When's it my turn♪

108
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,560
♪Wouldn't I love♪

109
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,320
♪Love to explore that♪

110
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:14,360
♪World up above♪

111
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,040
So good!

112
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:21,680
♪Part of that world♪

113
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,240
That was amazing!

114
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,360
Seriously, so good.

115
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,240
After we leave,

116
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,000
we're doing karaoke.

117
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:28,720
For sure.

118
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,160
We'll get a huge room

119
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,520
and just sing.

120
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,520
Karaoke showdown.

121
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,720
Losers drink tea.

122
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:34,680
Yeah.

123
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,880
We'll score each other,

124
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:38,480
in teams,

125
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,280
losers drink tea.

126
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,000
Exactly.

127
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,600
Maybe jasmine tea?

128
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,360
Sure.

129
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:47,560
Anyone home?

130
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,200
Someone's back.

131
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:49,740
Hello!

132
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,080
Hello.

133
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:55,300
(Turns to look)

134
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,800
Look at this.

135
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,200
Is that the beef soup you made?

136
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,820
(Beef soup)
Yeah.

137
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,440
Want to peel some garlic?

138
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:04,840
Sure.

139
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:06,720
(Helping)
Want me to peel some garlic?

140
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:08,040
For us.

141
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,200
How do you want the garlic?

142
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,840
Whole cloves?

143
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,880
Maybe another...

144
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,800
Three or four.

145
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:20,100
(Smacks)

146
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,540
(Smacks again)

147
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:25,540
(Watching closely)

148
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:27,520
Is this okay?

149
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,040
You just smash it like that?

150
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,880
Isn't that way faster?

151
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:32,680
True.

152
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,520
You want it like that?

153
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,200
Just mince it.

154
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,160
I'm going

155
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:41,120
to give it a quick fry later.

156
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,320
That brings out the flavor.

157
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,000
A few more cloves, right?

158
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,400
Yeah, that's good.

159
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,060
(Chopping garlic)

160
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:55,680
What's this soup called?

161
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,140
(Adds apple)

162
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,560
It's not really soup.

163
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,520
It's...

164
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:02,880
just clear-braised beef ribs.

165
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:03,600
You can

166
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,520
drink the broth too.

167
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,880
I'll make a dipping sauce

168
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:07,640
for the beef.

169
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,280
Never had it?

170
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:08,720
No.

171
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,480
(Curious)
Why add apple?

172
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,280
For more flavor.

173
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,320
It makes it really savory.

174
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,300
(Smiles)

175
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:18,160
Yesterday's turned out great.

176
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,200
Okay.

177
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,120
I'll tweak it today.

178
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:20,920
I'll add some pears.

179
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,160
Huh?

180
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,720
Pears.

181
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,040
I totally misheard you.

182
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,180
Oh my God.

183
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:29,840
(Stares)

184
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:30,980
(Asks)
Do you cook often?

185
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,960
Sometimes when I'm bored,

186
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,160
cooking's really relaxing.

187
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,680
I just love hearing it bubble.

188
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:37,260
(Nods)

189
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,800
I used to cook on gas.

190
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,400
With this, I can't really...

191
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,080
Toss the wok?

192
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,680
Yeah. Not the same.

193
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:51,200
It stays here.

194
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,400
Because it's flat, right?

195
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,320
Right.

196
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,320
I can only stir it like this.

197
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:04,640
Okay, now I can really smell it.

198
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,300
(Teasing)
No lying.

199
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,440
Let's see if it needs anything.

200
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,200
Smell it.

201
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:09,960
Nothing else.

202
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,600
Did you add salt?

203
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,120
A little.

204
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,560
Smells great.

205
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,280
Try it.

206
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:18,640
My chopsticks are backward.

207
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,000
Good.

208
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:23,720
We're good, right?

209
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,660
(Praises it)

210
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:26,920
Then we're good.

211
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,480
Want some?

212
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:28,920
Yeah.

213
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:30,360
I'll get chopsticks.

214
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,640
Tastes just right.

215
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:35,960
It's so good.

216
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:38,580
(Hands it over)

217
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,320
It's a little bland.

218
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,320
Then add some salt.

219
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:50,680
Tastes fine to me.

220
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,600
Just a bit more salt.

221
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:56,400
Cucumber's a bit bland.

222
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,880
The shrimp's more flavorful.

223
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:00,080
A little more MSG.

224
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,000
So good.

225
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:05,500
(Looks)

226
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:07,620
(Laughs)

227
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,580
(Sighs)

228
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:14,280
(Concerned)
What's wrong?

229
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:15,940
(Concerned)
Nothing.

230
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:16,960
Take one more.

231
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:17,760
What's wrong?

232
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:21,120
I got up too early today, so...

233
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:21,640
Sleepy?

234
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:22,760
Early mornings mess me up.

235
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:24,280
I had a work meeting this morning.

236
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,600
When'd you go to bed?

237
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,480
Meetings all morning.

238
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,520
Go get some sleep.

239
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,560
Stop cooking.

240
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,040
I'm okay.

241
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:34,000
I'm just...

242
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,360
recharging.

243
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:38,300
(Recharging)

244
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,720
Let's poke it with a chopstick

245
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,240
and see if it's done.

246
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,040
Okay.

247
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:45,700
(Grabs chopsticks)

248
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,240
Okay, try it.

249
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:51,980
(Fans it)

250
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:52,800
Try it.

251
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,320
Try it.

252
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:58,400
It's hot.

253
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,320
It's done.

254
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:02,000
Should we take the pumpkin out?

255
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:02,680
And then...

256
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,920
I think so.

257
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,160
I've got it.

258
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:08,580
(Puts on gloves)

259
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,240
Okay, the rest...

260
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,200
It's hot.

261
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:20,000
This needs to go back in.

262
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Okay.

263
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:22,640
Applause.

264
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,360
Let's eat first.

265
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,160
Okay.

266
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,480
Doesn't this place feel dreamy?

267
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,120
- Yeah.
- Like you...

268
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:29,240
Just like you said.

269
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:29,600
Right?

270
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:29,960
Utopia.

271
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:30,960
Kind of like a utopia.

272
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,680
Look, come here.

273
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,040
Okay.

274
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,480
Yeah, these two buttons.

275
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,760
This one's for the stargazing room.

276
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:42,580
And one more.

277
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:44,740
(Wishing Fountain, Stargazing Room, City Date)
The right one is City Date.

278
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,720
That's pretty cool.

279
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,500
Yeah.

280
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,320
(Smiles)

281
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,560
And up ahead,

282
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:52,880
there's a kayak down there.

283
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,880
We can actually use it?

284
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:54,800
Yeah, we can.

285
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,920
Yeah, look.

286
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,020
(Warns)
Careful. It's slippery.

287
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,960
Usually,

288
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,040
it's two people per kayak,

289
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,000
facing each other.

290
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,000
That's nice.

291
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,320
But use bug spray before coming down.

292
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,040
So you don't get bitten.

293
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,420
(Concerned)

294
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:19,580
And this is the second space?

295
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:19,980
Yeah.

296
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,240
There are workout machines,

297
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,480
a climbing wall, and other equipment.

298
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:27,320
(Holds the door)
Thanks.

299
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:28,640
So cool.

300
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:29,240
Right?

301
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:30,230
Yeah.

302
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,780
Do you like things...

303
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:33,560
(Asks)

304
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:36,320
like rock climbing?

305
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,320
I've never tried rock climbing,

306
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,880
but I like hiking, horseback riding,

307
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,040
and swimming.

308
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,800
My work and daily life

309
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,840
are both in the city.

310
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:47,200
So when I have free time,

311
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,000
I usually either stay home

312
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,720
or exercise downstairs.

313
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,160
For me,

314
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:54,400
I'd go outdoors.

315
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,480
I'm in the city every day,

316
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,120
so work and life

317
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:58,680
blur together.

318
00:09:58,680 --> 00:09:59,360
Yeah, true.

319
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:04,080
This big sign is for you.

320
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,060
(Laughs)

321
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,000
Welcome, Xing.

322
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:06,900
(A new housemate is moving in tonight)

323
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:07,860
(Welcome, Xing)

324
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,400
How did you feel when I

325
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:20,320
first talked to you?

326
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,760
It felt so sudden.

327
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,640
Like...

328
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,440
Were you nervous?

329
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,760
Definitely.

330
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,400
I was worried my reaction

331
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,280
might not be

332
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:37,000
what you expected.

333
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:44,320
Did I make you feel that way before?

334
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:46,140
(Looks at her)

335
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:48,560
I knew you didn't dislike me.

336
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,800
I just thought you were quiet.

337
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:58,160
And then?

338
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:02,120
Then a lot changed really fast.

339
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,600
I felt like I couldn't...

340
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:07,740
(Looks at him)

341
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:11,320
take it too slow with you.

342
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,880
Do you think we're moving too fast?

343
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:23,440
(Asks)
Does that make you uncomfortable

344
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,120
at all?

345
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,320
No.

346
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,480
(Turns to look)
Actually,

347
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,080
once I started acting differently,

348
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,240
I felt

349
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,940
more at ease too.

350
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:35,820
(Looks)

351
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:38,200
Okay, as long as you're comfortable.

352
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,260
(Smiles)

353
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,520
For me,

354
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,520
once I get comfortable with someone,

355
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:46,680
I might talk less.

356
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,640
I think that's pretty normal.

357
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:52,440
We also might not get

358
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,120
that much time.

359
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,360
Later on,

360
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,280
I'll probably

361
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:57,560
spend more time

362
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:58,480
in the school lab.

363
00:11:58,800 --> 00:11:59,760
So I might not

364
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,560
reply right away.

365
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,880
Would that bother you

366
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,200
or make you want to see me?

367
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:05,860
(Asks)

368
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,480
I think...

369
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,560
even if we can't meet,

370
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,480
we should still stay...

371
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,920
For me, video calls

372
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,720
beat phone calls,

373
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,360
and calls beat texting.

374
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,400
Do you like video calls?

375
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,760
I love them.

376
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,720
What about you? Would it bug you?

377
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,640
No.

378
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,160
If I'm busy,

379
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,600
I might just prop my phone up.

380
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,360
That's fine.

381
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,640
With video calls,

382
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,120
just seeing their face

383
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,160
and having them there

384
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:41,320
feels like they're right beside you.

385
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,840
I want to go downstairs.

386
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,120
Okay, let's go.

387
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,280
This spot's nice too.

388
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,440
Sure. Anywhere's fine.

389
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:57,080
Here then.

390
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,200
Where do you want to sit?

391
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:58,920
Here.

392
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,100
(Looks)

393
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,740
What's your favorite movie?

394
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:07,600
(Asks)

395
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,080
My favorite...

396
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:12,200
I really love "Flipped"

397
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,520
and "A Little Thing Called Love".

398
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,160
I love animated movies too.

399
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:16,720
(Curious)
Like what?

400
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:17,880
"The Magician",

401
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:20,880
"Robot Dreams",

402
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,320
and "Your Name".

403
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,680
That one's a classic.

404
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:24,980
(Nods)

405
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,320
Those kinds of animated movies

406
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,440
just feel

407
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,520
really comforting.

408
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:31,120
Go on.

409
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:33,040
I like

410
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:33,800
"Love Letter".

411
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:36,360
That sounds familiar.

412
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:37,680
Have you seen

413
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,160
the film...

414
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,680
"Song of the Phoenix"?

415
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,440
It's about passing traditions down.

416
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,940
(Agrees)

417
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:45,880
Anything else?

418
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,920
There was a time

419
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:48,000
I was really into movies.

420
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:48,520
I...

421
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,240
I'd even go to the movies alone.

422
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:56,720
And when the characters

423
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,640
were celebrating, I'd toast

424
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,360
with them.

425
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,440
I'd go alone.

426
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,200
I'd watch movies by myself

427
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,400
and see two back-to-back.

428
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:07,960
Two movies?

429
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:08,520
Yeah.

430
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,560
I'd go after lunch,

431
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,120
stay until evening,

432
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,520
then grab dinner and head home.

433
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,720
Have you seen

434
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,920
Zhang Yashu's "Wind"?

435
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,240
No.

436
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,760
Look it up later.

437
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:22,600
I will.

438
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:25,680
She's surrounded by fans,

439
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:27,960
holding this huge sheer fabric,

440
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,160
and wearing

441
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,120
this really light dress.

442
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,880
The fabric moves in the wind,

443
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,400
and she's just...

444
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:34,400
so beautiful.

445
00:14:34,420 --> 00:14:36,300
(Nods)

446
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:39,640
Dance is just...

447
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:40,680
so captivating.

448
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,320
Really?

449
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,360
I mean, if you can dance.

450
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:44,000
If you can dance? Of course.

451
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,240
When I dance,

452
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:52,120
I feel the most confident.

453
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,800
Do I seem confident?

454
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,680
Very. You seem really confident.

455
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,600
Really?

456
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:57,720
Then I've changed.

457
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,040
I wasn't like that before.

458
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,640
My teacher used to say

459
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:02,720
I become someone else.

460
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,680
Offstage,

461
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:04,880
I was really withdrawn.

462
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:08,560
I was an introvert back then,

463
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,360
really quiet.

464
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:15,200
But onstage, I felt so free.

465
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:18,560
Now I kind of want to see you dance.

466
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,680
I'm looking forward to it.

467
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,400
What kind of food

468
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,520
are you into these days?

469
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:28,800
Probably more Cantonese food.

470
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,080
Cantonese?

471
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:31,600
Yeah, mostly.

472
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,480
Any Beijing restaurants

473
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:35,040
you'd recommend?

474
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:36,480
In Beijing?

475
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,560
Peking duck.

476
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,200
Peking duck is a restaurant?

477
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,040
I get chicken hot pot a lot.

478
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:43,640
Chicken hot pot

479
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:44,840
is Cantonese too?

480
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,120
Rapid-fire.

481
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:49,840
Name your top three dishes.

482
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:50,820
(Listens)

483
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,160
Mapo tofu.

484
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,840
Minced pork with long beans.

485
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:56,040
Minced pork with long beans?

486
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:01,120
Oh, minced pork with long beans?

487
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,800
Like a dry stir-fry?

488
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,640
Yeah, chopped up,

489
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:05,160
and they taste a little

490
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,680
pickled.

491
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,040
A little sour.

492
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,040
A little sour?

493
00:16:09,040 --> 00:16:10,200
Kind of like pickles.

494
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,360
It's really good.

495
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:12,600
And the third?

496
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,360
That's it?

497
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,040
The third one...

498
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,200
That rib dish...

499
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,440
What's it called?

500
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:18,000
Corn and ribs...

501
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,660
(Answers)
Corn and pork rib soup.

502
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:20,760
I love pork ribs.

503
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:24,280
And also...

504
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:26,040
beef brisket with tomatoes.

505
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:27,720
Tomato beef brisket?

506
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:28,840
With potatoes.

507
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,880
It gets nice and thick,

508
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:34,960
great with rice.

509
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,240
Mash the potatoes into it.

510
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,280
Exactly.

511
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:37,960
What about you?

512
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:38,655
(Asks back)

513
00:16:38,655 --> 00:16:39,860
What home-style dishes do you like?

514
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:40,920
Home-style dishes...

515
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,960
I like...

516
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,040
vinegar-style moo shu.

517
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:48,920
Wood ear mushrooms?

518
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:49,360
No.

519
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:52,760
It's egg and pork,

520
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,000
stir-fried and tangy.

521
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,160
So vinegar, egg, and pork?

522
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,080
Coke chicken wings.

523
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,000
Coconut chicken.

524
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:02,220
(Agrees)

525
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,120
I like boiled dishes.

526
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,320
So you prefer milder flavors?

527
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:07,040
Even boiled food

528
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,400
can be really flavorful.

529
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,120
And...

530
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,600
Drain the water, add seasoning,

531
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:12,320
then cook again?

532
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:13,600
There's a trick.

533
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,000
Teach me.

534
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,440
Not telling you.

535
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:19,940
(Teasing)

536
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:22,840
This...

537
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:27,800
I'll just make it for you.

538
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:29,820
(I'll just make it for you)

539
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,440
Just tell me when you want it.

540
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:41,480
Let's go.

541
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,800
Okay.

542
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,120
Is it good?

543
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,280
Yeah, pretty good.

544
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,600
Let me try some too.

545
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,680
It's like a soft...

546
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:55,360
cookie.

547
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:57,080
Where'd you guys go today?

548
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:58,400
Just downstairs,

549
00:17:58,400 --> 00:17:59,520
by the entrance.

550
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,400
Did you have fun today?

551
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:03,260
(Laughs)

552
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,990
You had a good time, right?

553
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:06,000
Yeah...

554
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,200
we slowly started talking more.

555
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,440
We're moving

556
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:11,200
at a really natural pace.

557
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,960
Going faster wouldn't suit you.

558
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:16,360
We're just letting things

559
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:20,320
move forward at this pace.

560
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:21,240
So...

561
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,480
It's good.

562
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:24,880
But it has to be someone

563
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:25,920
worth it.

564
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:28,560
Bravery isn't just rushing in.

565
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,400
Exactly.

566
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,080
It's kind of amazing,

567
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:37,240
you two being twins.

568
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:43,120
Were you shocked?

569
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:44,480
Very.

570
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:48,160
Have you met twins before?

571
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:49,640
Yeah.

572
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:50,800
I have,

573
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:51,880
but never this alike.

574
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,640
Maybe because you just met us.

575
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:54,960
That could be why.

576
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:56,240
But you two

577
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,280
each have your own vibe.

578
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,240
You look alike, but feel different.

579
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:03,720
So interesting.

580
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,320
Just like everyone here,

581
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:06,400
everyone's different.

582
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,200
Yeah.

583
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:11,680
So what's going on?

584
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:15,400
This is hard.

585
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,440
I saw you two talking.

586
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,040
Yeah.

587
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:20,680
I talked to him all night.

588
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:23,160
All night?

589
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:23,800
Yeah.

590
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,080
Honestly,

591
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,160
I feel like

592
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,640
we have more in common.

593
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,560
But right now,

594
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,920
I still want to get to know everyone.

595
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:35,480
It's too soon to decide,

596
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,120
and that worries me a little.

597
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:38,320
I agree.

598
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:40,080
Yeah. Just feel things out.

599
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,880
It's still early.

600
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,200
You need more time

601
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,780
to see what everyone's like.

602
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,840
Yeah.

603
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:52,440
We're having hot pot tomorrow.

604
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,440
How do you know?

605
